@startuml 05b-component-federated
title Federated layout — 2+ Super6c clusters + arbitrary nodes on L2

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo
skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
    BorderColor Black
}

package "Super6c #1 (ivalice)" {
    node "dalmasca (head)" as H1 {
        [slurmctld_1]
        [slurmdbd (federated)] as DBD
        [munge (shared key)] as MH1
        [nfs-server (local)] as NFSH1
        [slurmrestd] as RS1
    }
    node "workers .11-.15" as W1N
}

package "Super6c #2 (dalmaya)" {
    node "dalmaya (head)" as H2 {
        [slurmctld_2]
        [munge (shared key)] as MH2
        [nfs-server (local)] as NFSH2
        [slurmrestd] as RS2
    }
    node "workers .21-.25" as W2N
}

package "Arbitrary L2 node" as Arb {
    node "some-beefy-rig\n(x86_64 or aarch64)" as X {
        [slurmd] as SX
        [munge (shared key)] as MX
        [nfs client (one of the heads)] as NX
    }
}

package "Shared services (new)" {
    database "MinIO\n(artifacts, models, features)" as Min
    database "Postgres\n(experiment registry)" as PG
    [Federation controller\n(slurmdbd federation OR\nexternal meta-scheduler)] as FedCtrl
}

cloud "L2 switch / routed subnet" as L2

H1 -- L2
H2 -- L2
X  -- L2
Min -- L2
PG  -- L2

DBD --> FedCtrl : federation control plane
RS1 --> FedCtrl
RS2 --> FedCtrl

slurmctld_1 <--> slurmctld_2 : federated scheduling\n(native Slurm federation OR\nmeta-scheduler over REST)

W1N --> NFSH1 : cluster-local NFS
W2N --> NFSH2
NX  --> NFSH1 : (example mount;\none cluster at a time)

H1 <--> Min : s3-compatible\nget/put
H2 <--> Min
X  <--> Min
H1 <--> PG
H2 <--> PG

note right of FedCtrl
  **Two viable control-plane options (to be chosen
  based on real traffic):**
  (A) Native Slurm federation via slurmdbd,
      enabling `sbatch -M cluster_2`.
  (B) External meta-scheduler that submits to each
      cluster's slurmrestd over HTTP.
  Option A is simpler while homogeneous; option B
  scales to non-Slurm compute later.
end note

note bottom of Min
  **Content-hashed artifact store.** Models, .mfc,
  decode results keyed by sha256 so any cluster can
  hydrate without knowing where the bytes were made.
end note

note bottom of PG
  **Experiment registry.** Row per experiment:
  name, cfg hash, model hash, decode result hash,
  owner, origin cluster. Drives the "any head can
  show any experiment" UX.
end note

@enduml
